--
-- Test Description
-- This test checks the operation of the RX exposed FIFO interface (write).
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks the operation of the rx_w_mod signal
-- * Checks the operation of the rx_w_flush signal
-- * Checks the operation of the rx_w_status signal
-- * Checks the operation of the rx_w_overflow signal
-- * Checks the operation of the rx_w_err signal
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts, specific addresses
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 128-bit FIFO data bus.
--  3. Receive a frame of length 64 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
--  4. Receive a frame of length 65 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
--  5. Receive a frame of length 66 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
--  6. Receive a frame of length 67 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
--  7. Receive a frame of length 68 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
--  8. Receive a frame of length 69 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
--  9. Receive a frame of length 70 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 10. Receive a frame of length 71 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 11. Receive a frame of length 72 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 12. Receive a frame of length 73 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 13. Receive a frame of length 74 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 14. Receive a frame of length 75 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 15. Receive a frame of length 76 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 16. Receive a frame of length 77 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 17. Receive a frame of length 78 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 18. Receive a frame of length 79 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 19. Receive a frame of length 80 bytes, and verify that the rx_w_mod
--     signal indicates the correct number of bytes valid on the final write.
-- 20. Check statistics for above operations.
-- 21. Setup all address matching registers to the broadcast address 
--     (0xffffffffffff).
-- 22. Setup all type matching registers on the VLAN frame.
--     Note that the type field is after the VLAN tag and has value (0x4444)
--     in this example.
-- 23. Activate all four external match signals.
-- 24. Receive a 64 byte, broadcast, VLAN type frame. Verify that the 
--     rx_w_status output indicates matches on all address, type and external
--     bits. Also check that a broadcast frame is indicated, and that the
--     correct VLAN information is indicated on rx_w_status.
-- 25. Setup for multicast hash address matching. Set hash index register
--     to all ones and set the multicast hash enable in the network config
--     register. This will enable reception of all multicast addresses.
-- 26. Receive a 64 byte, multicast, VLAN type frame. Verify that the 
--     rx_w_status output indicates matches on all address, type and 
--     external bits. Also check that a multicast frame is indicated, and 
--     that the correct VLAN information is indicated on rx_w_status.
-- 27. Setup for unicast hash address matching. Set hash index register
--     to all ones and set the unicast hash enable in the network config
--     register.
-- 28. Receive a 64 byte, unicast, VLAN type frame. Verify that the rx_w_status
--     output indicates matches on all address, type and external bits. Also
--     check that a unicast frame is indicated, and that the correct VLAN
--     information is indicated on rx_w_status.
-- 29. Receive a 64 byte frame, but some point during reception force an
--     overflow indication using the rx_w_overflow external FIFO input.
--     Verify that the design indicates bad status on the final write and that
--     the rx_w_err signal is also forced high. Also check that an RX overflow
--     interrupt and status are reported.
-- 30. Check statistics for above operations.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------



--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
-- Configuration Requirements ..
requires ext_fifo_interface 1
requires emac_bus_width 128
requires dma_bus_width 128
wait_states 3
bus_grant_delay 3


--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts, specific addresses
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 128-bit FIFO data bus.
--******************************************************************************
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register

-- this is the event count that will initialize the scaler for event counts. it will cause any future scaling to only scale
-- the counts after start_scale
start_scale

apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbrd      30 00000000  -- check that all interrupts are now enabled
apbwr      88 12345678  -- specific address register 1 bottom
apbwr      8C 00001111  -- specific address register 1 top

-- # Initialize the network configuration register
-- #   -eam      <1|0|random>, default = 0. This is external address matching
-- #   -duplex   <full|half|random>, default = random
-- #   -speed    <1g|100m|10m|random>, default = random
-- #   -jumbo    <1|0|random>, default = random. This wont affect the RX transactor below, but will automatically cause jumbos to be dropped.
-- #   -copy_all <1|0|random>, default = 0. If 0, ensure you initialize the dest_addr in the rx transactor to something that will match
-- #   -databus  <32|64|128|take_from_cfg|random>, default = random, bus <= config.  The max value is the value set in dma_bus_width in gem_defs.v
-- #   -rx_toe   <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables RX TCP/IP checksum offload
-- #   -pcs_en   <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables SGMII PCS
-- #   -pause_en <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables pausing of transmission
-- #   -dont_copy_pause <1|0|random>, default = 0. Controls whether pause frames are copied
init_ncr -sgmii_en 0 -pcs_en 0 -retry_test 0 -copy_all 0 -duplex half -speed 100m -jumbo 0 -databus take_from_cfg -eam 0 -rx_toe 0 -pause_en 0 -dont_copy_pause 0 -multicast_hash 0 -unicast_hash 0

apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      00 zzzzzzzz repeat=15 -- repeat read 15 times to ensure rx enable is propagated through design



